1
00:00:03,350 --> 00:00:06,970
Kya aap jaante hain ki
Direct Tax aur Indirect Tax

2
00:00:07,010 --> 00:00:08,310
mein kya difference hota hai?

3
00:00:08,950 --> 00:00:14,570
Chaliye, ise daily life ke simple examples
se samajhte hain. Sabse pehle, Direct Tax.

4
00:00:15,270 --> 00:00:20,950
Jab kisi individual ki income ya kisi
company ke profit par directly tax lagta hai

5
00:00:21,009 --> 00:00:27,549
toh use Direct Tax kehte hain. Jaise –
Income Tax aur Corporate Tax.

6
00:00:32,178 --> 00:00:33,198
Aur Indirect Tax.

7
00:00:33,658 --> 00:00:39,438
Jab hum koi samaan kharidte hain ya koi
service avail karte hain, toh us par lagne wale tax ko

8
00:00:39,518 --> 00:00:45,158
Indirect Tax kehte hain. Iska sabse common
example hai GST – Goods and Services Tax.

9
00:00:45,618 --> 00:00:49,938
Lekin sawaal hai ki ise
Indirect Tax kyun kehte hain?

10
00:00:50,678 --> 00:00:56,038
Kyunki ismein tax government ko directly
customer nahi de raha. Iske bajay, seller

11
00:00:56,118 --> 00:01:01,758
ya service provider customer se tax
collect karke government ko deposit karte hain.

12
00:01:01,818 --> 00:01:07,218
Yaani tax collect karne aur government
tak pahunchane ke beech mein ek intermediary

13
00:01:07,258 --> 00:01:12,418
hota hai. Jaise, jab aap restaurant mein
khana khate hain, toh applicable GST aapke bill

14
00:01:12,498 --> 00:01:16,838
mein include hota hai, jise restaurant
government ko deposit karta hai. Toh

15
00:01:16,878 --> 00:01:19,278
ab dono ke beech ka difference samajhiye.

16
00:01:23,326 --> 00:01:27,866
Direct Tax mein tax directly income
ya profit par lagta hai, jabki Indirect

17
00:01:27,905 --> 00:01:33,066
Tax goods aur services par lagta hai aur
ise customer indirectly pay karta hai.

18
00:01:33,106 --> 00:01:37,045
Toh agar yeh video aapko achchi lagi ho toh
channel ko follow karein. Thank you.
